  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pagehead-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">About us</span>
      <h1>We stay through the years that follow.</h1>
      <div class="lede"><p>Strandfold is a survivor-led support organisation working at the point where crisis response ends and long-term recovery begins.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-lg">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid g-2" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
        <h2 class="display-caps">Nobody was answering the rest.</h2>
        <div class="imgslot is-empty" style="--ratio:3 / 2" role="img" aria-label="Story image — not yet added"><div class="imgslot-inner"><svg class="imgslot-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="9.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-4.5-4.5L11 16l-2-2-5 5"/></svg><p class="imgslot-label">Story image</p><p class="imgslot-hint">3:2 · 1200 × 800px</p><p class="imgslot-note">A room, a doorway, a desk. Not a person who came to you for help.</p></div></div>      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Strandfold Support Foundation began with <strong>[founding moment — a case, a realisation, a gap someone witnessed]</strong>. In <strong>[year]</strong>, <strong>[founder / founding group]</strong> started with <strong>[modest starting point — a phone line, a room, a WhatsApp group]</strong>.</p>
<p>What became clear early was this: the women who reached out were rarely asking to be rescued. They were asking practical questions.</p>        <blockquote class="pullquote">Where can I sleep tonight with three children? Can he take the house? If I report it, what happens to my job? Who is going to pay for a lawyer?</blockquote>
        <p>Emergency response answered the first question. Nobody was answering the rest.</p>
<p><strong>Strandfold was built to answer the rest.</strong></p>
<p>Today we serve <strong>[number]</strong> women a year across <strong>[locations]</strong>, with <strong>[number]</strong> staff and <strong>[number]</strong> trained volunteers.</p>      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="redband">
  <div class="split">
    <div class="split-body">
      <span class="eyebrow">The name</span>
      <h2 class="display-caps">Why we’re called Strandfold</h2>
      <p>A single strand is fragile. Pull it and it breaks. But strands folded together — twisted, layered, held — become rope strong enough to carry weight that would snap any one of them alone.</p>
<p>The older sense of <strong>fold</strong> is a shelter: an enclosure where the vulnerable are kept through the night, not forever, but long enough for morning.</p>
<p>That is the work. Not rescue. Not charity. A place to be held, and enough hands folded together to carry what one woman was never meant to carry by herself.</p>    </div>
    <div class="split-visual">
      <div class="imgslot imgslot-fill is-empty" style="--ratio:4 / 3" role="img" aria-label="Band image — not yet added"><div class="imgslot-inner"><svg class="imgslot-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="9.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-4.5-4.5L11 16l-2-2-5 5"/></svg><p class="imgslot-label">Band image</p><p class="imgslot-hint">4:3 · 1200 × 900px</p><p class="imgslot-note">Abstract or environmental.</p></div></div>    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-lg">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our approach</span>
    <h2 class="display-caps">Built around how trauma actually behaves.</h2>
    <div class="grid g-2" style="margin-top:2.25rem;gap:2rem">
            <div class="card">
        <h3>Trauma-informed, always</h3>
        <p>Our team is trained to recognise that trauma changes how a person remembers, speaks, trusts and decides. A survivor who tells her story out of order is not lying. A survivor who returns to her abuser has not failed.</p>
<p>We build our processes around how trauma actually behaves, not around how we wish it behaved.</p>      </div>
            <div class="card">
        <h3>Survivor-led, not survivor-managed</h3>
        <p>Women who have come through our programmes sit on our advisory board and shape our services. The people closest to the problem are closest to the solution.</p>      </div>
            <div class="card">
        <h3>We do not pressure anyone to leave</h3>
        <p>This is the hardest thing to explain to donors and the most important thing we do. On average, a woman attempts to leave an abusive relationship several times before it holds.</p>
<p>Each attempt is information, not failure. A woman who knows we will still be here when she returns is a woman who eventually comes back for the last time.</p>      </div>
            <div class="card">
        <h3>Confidentiality without exception</h3>
        <p>We do not share names, case files, photographs or identifying details with anyone — media, donors, family, employers — without explicit written consent, which can be withdrawn at any moment.</p>      </div>
          </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-lg" style="background:var(--white);border-block:1px solid var(--rule)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Core values</span>
    <h2 class="display-caps">Five things we hold to.</h2>
    <div class="grid g-2" style="margin-top:2.25rem;gap:2rem 3rem">
            <div class="feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M4 21c0-4 3.6-6 8-6s8 2 8 6"/></svg>        <div>
          <h3>She Leads</h3>
          <p>The survivor decides. We do not decide for her, pressure her to leave, or withdraw support if she returns. We provide options, information and honesty, and we respect the choice she makes with them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
            <div class="feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg>        <div>
          <h3>Confidentiality Is Sacred</h3>
          <p>What is shared with us stays with us. No names, no photographs, no case details without explicit, written, revocable consent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
            <div class="feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7.5-4.6-7.5-10A4.5 4.5 0 0 1 12 8a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 7.5 3c0 5.4-7.5 10-7.5 10Z"/></svg>        <div>
          <h3>Dignity Over Pity</h3>
          <p>We do not trade in tragedy for donations. No shock imagery. No woman is asked to perform her worst day to be worth helping.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
            <div class="feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 7 9.5 17.5 4 12"/></svg>        <div>
          <h3>Practical Over Performative</h3>
          <p>Awareness campaigns do not pay rent. Every programme must produce a measurable change in a woman’s safety, health, legal standing or income.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
            <div class="feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg>        <div>
          <h3>The Long Walk</h3>
          <p>Recovery is not an event. We measure success in years, not rescues.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
          </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-lg">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid g-2" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">What we don’t do</span>
        <h2 class="display-caps">Honesty builds more trust than a long list of claims.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="checklist">
                <li>We are <strong>not an emergency service</strong>. In immediate danger, call [emergency number].</li>
                <li>We do not operate our own shelter [or: our shelter has limited capacity]. We refer to vetted partner facilities.</li>
                <li>We are <strong>not a law firm</strong>. We provide legal guidance, documentation support and accompaniment, and connect you with practising counsel.</li>
                <li>We do not confront, contact or negotiate with abusers.</li>
                <li>We do not provide financial support for legal fees beyond [scope].</li>
              </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

